WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.336
[♪ theme music playing]

00:24.316 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:30.614
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:30.697 --> 00:32.241
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:32.324 --> 00:33.951
ANIMALS WERE FILMED
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE RULES

00:34.243 --> 00:35.327
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

00:35.410 --> 00:38.247
If I just left,
he'd lose it and cause trouble.

00:38.330 --> 00:40.999
It seemed like he'd do anything
to find that house's owner.

00:42.084 --> 00:43.085
Also...

00:44.253 --> 00:47.714
Even if it didn't end well with him,
he was hurt in front of me.

00:49.716 --> 00:50.717
Wait.

00:51.176 --> 00:52.552
Last time,

00:53.887 --> 00:56.098
didn't you say to team up with Wooju
if push came to shove?

00:56.723 --> 00:57.724
I did.

00:58.600 --> 00:59.601
Right.

01:00.394 --> 01:01.395
I said that.

01:01.478 --> 01:02.479
So what's with you?

01:05.274 --> 01:07.317
Why are you so angry?

01:10.070 --> 01:11.071
Well...

01:13.031 --> 01:14.825
Maybe it's because I like you.

01:17.786 --> 01:19.538
I don't like seeing you with another guy.

01:19.621 --> 01:21.248
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

01:27.462 --> 01:28.463
Why?

01:29.047 --> 01:30.299
What?

01:31.675 --> 01:32.676
I mean...

01:33.885 --> 01:36.513
Why should I give a reason
for liking someone?

01:36.597 --> 01:37.598
Why me?

01:38.682 --> 01:42.102
Legally speaking, I'm a divorcée.

01:42.185 --> 01:43.395
So I can't like you?

01:44.438 --> 01:46.648
Your family will obviously disapprove.

01:47.149 --> 01:49.901
Are you dating my family?
You'd be dating me.

01:50.569 --> 01:51.570
Even so.

01:53.697 --> 01:55.198
[♪ enthralling orchestral music playing]

01:55.282 --> 01:56.283
What about you?

01:56.867 --> 01:57.868
Sorry?

01:59.244 --> 02:01.621
Does it bother you that I like you?

02:02.622 --> 02:04.499
[hesitates] Well, no.

02:04.583 --> 02:06.626
I mean, it's not that I'm bothered.

02:07.169 --> 02:09.379
If I fall for you,

02:09.463 --> 02:11.757
I can't separate dating from marriage.

02:11.840 --> 02:14.760
But marriage comes
with real-life problems,

02:14.843 --> 02:17.262
and real life is always about money,

02:17.346 --> 02:19.681
so do you have some saved up?

02:20.140 --> 02:21.391
[♪ whimsical sting]

02:21.475 --> 02:22.726
I mean...

02:22.809 --> 02:25.604
I can tell from how you dress
that you're not the saving type.

02:25.687 --> 02:26.688
What?

02:27.397 --> 02:28.649
I dressed up today

02:28.732 --> 02:32.110
only because we were supposed
to meet up for lunch.

02:32.194 --> 02:34.363
I don't usually shop for clothes much.

02:34.446 --> 02:36.907
Oh, eating out with me. I see.

02:36.990 --> 02:38.325
[♪ gripping, whimsical music playing]

02:38.408 --> 02:39.910
Where do you live, then?

02:39.993 --> 02:40.994
At my grandmother's.

02:41.078 --> 02:42.371
Oh, with her.

02:42.454 --> 02:44.706
Oh, should I move out? I totally can.

02:44.790 --> 02:46.083
What? Oh, no.

02:46.708 --> 02:49.795
A subscription deposit is a must.
Do you have an account?

02:49.878 --> 02:51.630
No, because I lived abroad.

02:52.255 --> 02:53.632
-I see.
-I can open one.

02:55.592 --> 02:58.220
Are you afraid [gulps]

02:58.720 --> 03:02.140
I'll ask you to let me
stay with you in the unit you won?

03:02.933 --> 03:03.934
With me?

03:04.434 --> 03:05.602
[gasps softly]

03:05.686 --> 03:06.687
That must be it.

03:07.562 --> 03:09.106
Is that what you think of me?

03:09.606 --> 03:11.024
It's not like that.

03:11.108 --> 03:14.903
It's a bit embarrassing
to have to say this myself,

03:14.986 --> 03:16.780
but I'm not that badly off.

03:16.863 --> 03:18.532
I make a decent amount, too.

03:19.825 --> 03:21.493
I didn't think so of you, but you're...

03:21.576 --> 03:22.994
Me what?

03:23.745 --> 03:24.955
I just...

03:25.038 --> 03:29.751
It's just that I heard something
so unexpected and...

03:29.835 --> 03:30.836
I got flustered.

03:30.919 --> 03:33.296
Don't you think
you're going a bit too far?

03:33.755 --> 03:35.715
Did I ask you to marry me right away?

03:35.799 --> 03:38.301
I didn't expect to tell you
my feelings today, but I did,

03:38.385 --> 03:40.011
and I'm just as flustered.

03:40.429 --> 03:42.681
Gosh, I'm too scared to say anything else.

03:43.432 --> 03:45.058
What happened here just now...

03:45.851 --> 03:47.436
-Let's say it never happened.
-What?

03:47.978 --> 03:49.354
What? Wait, no.

03:49.438 --> 03:51.648
How can I pretend I didn't hear that?

03:51.731 --> 03:53.442
I was just too flustered.

03:53.525 --> 03:55.360
-Also, I'm a mess because I stayed up--
-It's fine.

03:55.444 --> 03:57.737
-Say you didn't hear a thing.
-I'm not rejecting...

03:57.821 --> 03:59.614
-Are you ticked off?
-Me?

03:59.698 --> 04:00.949
-Of course not.
-You are.

04:01.032 --> 04:02.409
[line ringing]

04:05.245 --> 04:06.872
[breathing heavily]

04:11.793 --> 04:14.504
[automated voice] The call can't
be connected. Transferring to voicemail.

04:14.588 --> 04:17.007
-[line disconnects]
-Geez, where did those two go?

04:22.345 --> 04:23.638
Meri!

04:24.514 --> 04:25.932
Meri. [sobbing]

04:27.225 --> 04:28.393
Why are you out here?

04:28.477 --> 04:30.604
I looked for you everywhere.

04:31.188 --> 04:33.148
Why did you leave a patient on his own?

04:33.231 --> 04:34.441
[sighs softly]

04:38.361 --> 04:39.738
Who are you?

04:41.198 --> 04:42.282
I'm Ms. Yoo's acquaintance.

04:42.365 --> 04:43.366
[scoffs]

04:44.659 --> 04:45.660
Her acquaintance?

04:46.578 --> 04:48.038
You think I don't know who you are?

04:48.622 --> 04:49.623
[Kim Wooju] That's right.

04:49.706 --> 04:51.082
I'm the homeowner.

04:51.166 --> 04:52.459
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

04:52.542 --> 04:56.588
I needed a housekeeper anyway,
so I asked her for a favor.

04:57.422 --> 04:58.590
A housekeeper?

04:59.132 --> 05:01.301
That's a really neat trick.

05:01.384 --> 05:03.553
You'll use the house
as an excuse to hit on her?

05:03.637 --> 05:04.971
[Meri] Watch your language.

05:05.639 --> 05:07.432
He's a team leader for one of my clients.

05:07.516 --> 05:09.768
He's doing me a favor
because I'm struggling.

05:09.851 --> 05:11.686
Oh, he's a team leader?

05:12.854 --> 05:16.191
You're pretty nosy for a team leader,
looking out for a business partner.

05:16.274 --> 05:17.442
Thanks for the compliment.

05:18.109 --> 05:20.487
Since I'm being nosy,
I might as well interfere.

05:22.906 --> 05:24.241
No, don't you come closer.

05:25.492 --> 05:26.535
I'm a patient!

05:27.285 --> 05:29.162
Don't come any closer!

05:29.246 --> 05:30.747
That hurts! Let go of me!

05:30.831 --> 05:32.999
You'll make the break even worse!

05:33.083 --> 05:34.459
-Be quiet.
-[exhales]

05:34.835 --> 05:35.961
Darn it!

05:36.044 --> 05:37.045
[phone vibrates]

05:40.549 --> 05:43.051
[Songhee] Ms. Yoo,
you need to come over right away.

05:43.134 --> 05:46.179
The coffee shop owner
doesn't like the logo we designed.

05:46.263 --> 05:49.307
You should go. I'll stay with him.

05:49.391 --> 05:51.059
What? Gosh, no.

05:51.142 --> 05:52.978
I can't ask that of you. It's fine.

05:53.395 --> 05:55.522
Songhee seems to need you really urgently.

05:56.064 --> 05:57.065
But still...

05:57.148 --> 05:59.234
I'd feel more comfortable if you left.

06:01.945 --> 06:04.155
Can you do that for me, then?

06:04.239 --> 06:05.699
His family will be here soon.

06:05.782 --> 06:06.783
Okay.

06:07.492 --> 06:09.160
You can't go, Meri. I'm a patient.

06:09.703 --> 06:12.038
Who knows what he might do to me?

06:12.122 --> 06:14.875
You're much safer with him
than with me. Don't worry.

06:15.417 --> 06:16.835
Thanks a lot, Mr. Kim.

06:17.335 --> 06:18.712
-Bye.
-Meri!

06:19.421 --> 06:20.422
[groans softly]

06:20.797 --> 06:22.465
Meri! Let go of me!

06:22.549 --> 06:24.759
Let me go. Meri!

06:24.843 --> 06:26.511
[patient] What's all this goddamn noise?

06:28.096 --> 06:29.222
Do you own this place?

06:29.306 --> 06:30.891
[♪ dramatic music playing]

06:30.974 --> 06:32.100
Keep it down.

06:42.569 --> 06:45.488
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

06:45.572 --> 06:47.490
EPISODE 7

06:49.409 --> 06:50.702
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

06:50.785 --> 06:53.163
I was sorting out
my late husband's things.

06:53.663 --> 06:55.665
This was deep inside the drawer.

06:57.208 --> 06:59.044
It seemed important.

07:05.425 --> 07:07.927
CHAIRWOMAN KO PHILNYUN

07:08.011 --> 07:10.430
If Mr. Ko took this home to work on it...

07:12.515 --> 07:14.768
someone in the company could be involved.

07:16.519 --> 07:17.520
Look into it quietly.

07:18.480 --> 07:19.481
I'll do that.

07:19.689 --> 07:21.066
[knock at door, door opens]

07:24.027 --> 07:25.028
[door closes]

07:27.781 --> 07:29.032
[♪ music crescendos]

07:39.876 --> 07:41.252
[♪ music stops]

07:41.336 --> 07:43.838
It's the licensing details
for the plant in Texas.

07:45.507 --> 07:48.551
Construction is going exactly as planned.

07:49.260 --> 07:51.012
Once it's complete within the year,

07:51.096 --> 07:54.432
we'll run seven production lines
for testing purposes.

07:54.516 --> 07:57.644
The dorms for the local employees
will open sometime next month.

07:58.812 --> 08:00.897
Allocate plenty of time for testing,

08:00.980 --> 08:03.191
and train the bakers and employees well.

08:03.942 --> 08:06.861
The Kaltz Hotel is
one of the top US hotel chains.

08:07.404 --> 08:09.614
We can't afford to make a mistake
while supplying them.

08:09.698 --> 08:11.324
Yes, I understand.

08:11.408 --> 08:13.910
What time are we meeting
Director David from Kaltz?

08:13.993 --> 08:15.120
We can leave soon.

08:17.372 --> 08:21.042
I looked around the US plant
with Director Jang last month.

08:21.126 --> 08:22.377
I see.

08:22.460 --> 08:24.379
With a plant that size,

08:24.462 --> 08:28.633
you can supply the buffet
at all our hotels at once.

08:29.050 --> 08:30.343
Sure.

08:30.427 --> 08:32.929
You have 320 hotels in North America,

08:33.012 --> 08:35.849
and we can't send our experts
to each of them.

08:35.932 --> 08:39.394
We decided to go out on a limb
and open a plant.

08:39.477 --> 08:41.271
[David in English] Yes, I heard about it.

08:41.354 --> 08:44.858
[in Korean] I heard you secured
major funding from an investment firm.

08:44.941 --> 08:47.944
We're supplying our hangwa desserts
to a top US hotel chain.

08:48.445 --> 08:52.115
We need them to live up
to Myungsoondang's reputation.

08:52.657 --> 08:54.075
[chuckles contentedly]

08:54.534 --> 08:58.663
I see the 80-year tradition
was built on hard work.

08:58.747 --> 09:01.708
Starting with the deal with our hotel,

09:01.791 --> 09:05.086
I hope Myungsoondang becomes
a household name throughout the US.

09:05.170 --> 09:08.214
Yes, I hope you'll help us with that.

09:08.298 --> 09:09.382
[all chuckle]

09:10.216 --> 09:11.301
-Please eat.
-Thank you.

09:12.052 --> 09:13.094
[cutlery clatters]

09:22.020 --> 09:24.939
I'll stay to discuss
a few more details with David.

09:25.023 --> 09:26.149
Keep up the good work.

09:26.691 --> 09:27.692
Goodbye.

09:37.744 --> 09:41.164
Would she ever contact Kaltz directly?

09:41.247 --> 09:42.332
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

09:42.415 --> 09:44.000
I quit that place a while ago.

09:44.084 --> 09:45.168
[chuckles]

09:45.251 --> 09:47.504
Don't worry.
Confirming the details is my job.

09:47.879 --> 09:49.172
[chuckles softly] Okay.

09:50.298 --> 09:52.884
I'm doing this because I trust you.

09:52.967 --> 09:57.013
By the way,
did you order to shut down J Consulting?

09:57.639 --> 09:59.599
Don't they still have some use?

09:59.682 --> 10:01.101
They've done enough.

10:01.601 --> 10:03.937
You should fly out right away.
Don't let anyone see you.

10:04.646 --> 10:05.647
Okay.

10:07.690 --> 10:08.858
[line ringing]

10:09.609 --> 10:12.654
Come on. Pick up, Meri.

10:12.737 --> 10:15.448
[automated voice] The call can't
be connected. Transferring to voicemail.

10:15.532 --> 10:16.533
-[sighs]
-[line disconnects]

10:16.616 --> 10:17.951
MERI

10:18.034 --> 10:19.285
[door slides open]

10:23.164 --> 10:24.165
[sighs]

10:27.085 --> 10:28.128
MYUNGSOONDANG

10:34.884 --> 10:36.469
You're giving bread to a patient?

10:37.011 --> 10:38.179
Don't eat if you don't want to.

10:39.556 --> 10:40.557
[sighs wearily]

10:40.640 --> 10:43.476
I'm not pleased
that I have to bring you food.

10:49.732 --> 10:50.859
[hums in satisfaction]

10:55.572 --> 10:56.698
[hums in satisfaction]

10:56.906 --> 10:57.949
[stomach rumbles]

10:58.032 --> 10:59.659
MILK

11:00.285 --> 11:01.286
Darn it.

11:09.169 --> 11:10.253
[coughing]

11:12.380 --> 11:13.381
[sighs]

11:13.715 --> 11:14.799
[clears throat]

11:16.509 --> 11:17.510
So...

11:18.136 --> 11:19.596
Is your name also Wooju?

11:19.679 --> 11:20.680
That's what Meri called you.

11:21.181 --> 11:23.391
Yes, unfortunately.

11:23.474 --> 11:25.059
It's more unfortunate for me.

11:26.394 --> 11:29.898
You don't seem to know about me and Meri.

11:29.981 --> 11:32.108
We skipped the wedding,
but we're practically married.

11:32.192 --> 11:33.401
We dated for five years.

11:33.943 --> 11:34.986
[scoffs softly]

11:35.278 --> 11:37.030
How much could you know about her?

11:37.238 --> 11:39.991
You say that about her
when you cheated on her?

11:40.700 --> 11:41.993
Geez, you're utter trash.

11:42.076 --> 11:43.077
What? Tra...

11:44.037 --> 11:45.038
It wasn't...

11:46.915 --> 11:47.916
It wasn't cheating.

11:49.876 --> 11:51.085
Momentary confusion.

11:51.586 --> 11:54.547
Okay? A man's temporary drift
brought upon by cold feet.

11:55.924 --> 11:57.175
You're a guy, too. You must get it.

11:57.967 --> 11:58.968
I don't get it.

12:00.136 --> 12:03.389
I only know how responsible
a man feels before marriage.

12:03.932 --> 12:04.933
[huffs]

12:05.266 --> 12:06.267
[inhales deeply]

12:07.393 --> 12:09.229
Try as you might. You can't beat me.

12:09.646 --> 12:10.647
Do you know why?

12:11.814 --> 12:12.815
Meri...

12:15.151 --> 12:16.319
cares about looks.

12:16.903 --> 12:17.904
She's a visual stan.

12:18.154 --> 12:19.864
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

12:20.615 --> 12:21.616
[scoffs]

12:21.950 --> 12:22.951
Hey.

12:23.826 --> 12:25.161
Wipe your mouth, will you?

12:26.204 --> 12:27.205
[huffs]

12:27.288 --> 12:28.623
You're too kind for your own good.

12:38.258 --> 12:40.134
[♪ dreamy, ambient music playing]

12:42.345 --> 12:43.346
What about you?

12:44.639 --> 12:45.640
Sorry?

12:45.723 --> 12:48.059
Does it bother you that I like you?

12:49.102 --> 12:51.271
Why did he grab my hand?

12:55.775 --> 12:57.610
The way he grabbed it

12:59.028 --> 13:00.488
made me freeze.

13:02.240 --> 13:06.452
[sighing in frustration]
What on earth did I say to his face?

13:11.541 --> 13:12.542
[phone chimes]

13:24.429 --> 13:26.514
[Kim Wooju] I'm leaving now.
Kim Wooju is asleep.

13:26.597 --> 13:29.851
Nothing much happened,
so don't worry and have a good night.

13:31.269 --> 13:32.395
[phone vibrates]

13:34.230 --> 13:35.315
[Meri] Thank you.

13:35.398 --> 13:37.066
Have a good night.

13:42.155 --> 13:43.740
I WON'T DO ANYTHING TO BOTHER YOU AGAIN

13:43.823 --> 13:44.824
[phone vibrates]

13:49.579 --> 13:52.707
I won't do anything to bother you again.

13:54.709 --> 13:55.918
[chuckles softly]

13:57.086 --> 13:58.296
[sighs contentedly]

14:05.887 --> 14:06.929
[siren wailing]

14:08.139 --> 14:09.348
[phone vibrating]

14:10.016 --> 14:12.852
Hello, ma'am. Are you getting treated?

14:14.437 --> 14:15.563
That's good to hear.

14:16.147 --> 14:18.858
You can't jog for a while, though.

14:20.985 --> 14:22.070
-Dinner?
-[indistinct chatter]

14:22.653 --> 14:23.905
What on earth--

14:28.034 --> 14:29.202
What the heck?

14:29.285 --> 14:31.996
-[Wooju's mom] Which way do we go?
-I don't know. Let's go upstairs.

14:33.164 --> 14:34.665
[both continue indistinctly]

14:37.085 --> 14:38.377
Yes, go on.

14:39.170 --> 14:40.588
[♪ tense, whimsical music playing]

14:42.090 --> 14:44.050
Do I need this shot?

14:44.133 --> 14:45.426
Yes, you do.

14:45.510 --> 14:46.636
-Be gentle.
-I will.

14:46.719 --> 14:47.970
-I'll be gentle.
-Be nice.

14:48.054 --> 14:49.347
It's just a small prick.

14:50.098 --> 14:51.724
[exclaiming in pain]

14:52.850 --> 14:54.393
Well done.

14:54.477 --> 14:57.230
Hold onto this and rub for a while.

14:57.313 --> 14:59.190
Lean forward so I can pull up your pants.

15:02.318 --> 15:03.402
Oh, come on!

15:03.486 --> 15:05.071
-We're done. Good for you.
-Thanks.

15:06.239 --> 15:07.573
[music increases in tempo]

15:12.370 --> 15:13.538
[♪ dramatic sting]

15:14.163 --> 15:16.124
-Can I have a word?
-Yes.

15:17.291 --> 15:20.128
He smells really bad.

15:20.503 --> 15:22.922
He's causing the others some discomfort.

15:23.798 --> 15:25.925
-Will you do something?
-Yes, sure.

15:33.850 --> 15:35.268
What did she whisper to you?

15:35.351 --> 15:36.602
When did you last shower?

15:37.895 --> 15:40.398
[patient 1] Staying clean
is crucial when you're ill.

15:40.481 --> 15:41.774
[complains indistinctly]

15:41.858 --> 15:44.861
-[patient 1] Or you start to smell.
-[patient 2] That's a huge nuisance.

15:48.447 --> 15:50.074
You're stinking up the room.

15:50.783 --> 15:52.451
You're being a nuisance to the others.

15:53.411 --> 15:54.829
I don't smell that bad.

15:57.415 --> 15:58.416
Not so rough.

16:02.670 --> 16:04.630
I have sensitive skin.

16:05.173 --> 16:07.717
My skin turns red if you rub too hard.

16:08.217 --> 16:09.343
Hey!

16:09.427 --> 16:10.511
Get this off my face!

16:11.095 --> 16:12.722
[screams] Hey!

16:12.805 --> 16:14.223
Wooju! Mom's here, darling!

16:14.307 --> 16:17.185
-My gosh.
-Wooju! I'm here.

16:17.268 --> 16:20.438
-My poor baby.
-Mom!

16:20.521 --> 16:21.981
My dear baby.

16:22.064 --> 16:23.524
Who did this to you?

16:23.608 --> 16:25.067
Who was it?

16:27.069 --> 16:28.654
[♪ dramatic music playing]

16:31.407 --> 16:33.743
Since you're here, I'll see myself out.

16:35.995 --> 16:37.121
[clears throat]

16:40.333 --> 16:41.584
[Wooju crying] Mom!

16:41.667 --> 16:43.878
[Wooju's mom crying] Wooju.
My darling boy. My baby.

16:43.961 --> 16:45.338
It must hurt so bad.

16:46.297 --> 16:49.217
[Wooju] That punk said I smelled!

16:50.593 --> 16:52.094
-[Wooju's sister] This much?
-A bit higher.

16:52.178 --> 16:54.013
-Higher.
-[Wooju's sister] Higher?

16:54.096 --> 16:55.097
[in English] Okay, stop.

16:55.514 --> 16:56.974
-[groans]
-Goodness.

16:57.892 --> 16:59.977
I'm glad it's a slight fracture.

17:00.394 --> 17:01.479
How did it happen?

17:03.022 --> 17:04.440
Was Meri involved?

17:05.024 --> 17:06.525
You went to see her that day.

17:07.818 --> 17:08.945
What is she talking about?

17:10.404 --> 17:11.864
[in Korean] I went to apologize to her.

17:12.406 --> 17:13.824
You screamed at her mom

17:13.908 --> 17:15.952
-and threw her food and stuff.
-You bet.

17:16.035 --> 17:19.288
Should I have apologized
that my son cheated?

17:19.747 --> 17:22.166
What do you think
Meri's mom would've done, then?

17:22.250 --> 17:24.335
She'd have demanded
we hand over the housing deposit.

17:24.418 --> 17:27.463
I got the upper hand before she could.

17:28.047 --> 17:29.090
Okay, fine.

17:29.173 --> 17:30.841
Why would you apologize to her anyway?

17:32.468 --> 17:33.594
Are you...

17:34.637 --> 17:36.305
Do you want to get back with her?

17:36.389 --> 17:37.765
[Wooju's mom] Wooju.

17:37.848 --> 17:39.100
Tell us the truth.

17:39.809 --> 17:40.851
What about Jenny?

17:40.935 --> 17:41.936
We broke up.

17:42.770 --> 17:43.938
-What?
-What?

17:44.021 --> 17:45.648
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

17:45.731 --> 17:47.358
My goodness.

17:47.441 --> 17:49.902
She seduced you only to two-time you?

17:49.986 --> 17:52.071
She should be punished for--

17:52.697 --> 17:53.864
[sputters]

17:53.948 --> 17:55.992
-[chuckling]
-Sorry.

17:56.701 --> 17:57.702
My bad. [chuckling]

17:58.578 --> 18:00.621
[Wooju's mom] Be more careful,
will you? [chuckles]

18:01.539 --> 18:02.623
You're right, Mom.

18:05.418 --> 18:07.044
I think I'm being punished.

18:07.545 --> 18:09.213
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

18:10.256 --> 18:11.382
[breath trembling]

18:12.383 --> 18:13.551
[crying] Mom.

18:15.428 --> 18:17.430
I think I really loved Meri.

18:19.390 --> 18:21.434
I don't think I can live without her.

18:23.686 --> 18:24.687
Mom.

18:25.521 --> 18:29.191
Can you go apologize to her
and bring her back?

18:30.318 --> 18:32.236
If Meri leaves me,

18:32.320 --> 18:34.947
I might just go somewhere and die!

18:35.031 --> 18:36.532
[wailing]

18:40.161 --> 18:42.705
Sorry, I'm working right now.

18:43.664 --> 18:45.249
Can't you do something?

18:45.791 --> 18:50.129
From what Wooju said,
he practically got hurt because of you.

18:52.256 --> 18:53.257
Hey, you.

18:53.341 --> 18:55.217
You're a mean thing, you.

18:55.843 --> 18:59.055
How can you ignore someone
you used to be so close to?

18:59.138 --> 19:02.808
We used to be close, which is why
I looked after him while you were away.

19:03.684 --> 19:05.728
I've done my duty.

19:06.228 --> 19:09.023
You said we were a bad match
and told me to get lost.

19:10.399 --> 19:13.361
I don't want to see you or Wooju again.

19:14.945 --> 19:16.030
I'll hang up now.

19:17.573 --> 19:18.574
[line disconnects]

19:21.494 --> 19:22.995
[♪ melancholy music playing]

19:25.122 --> 19:26.457
[sighs]

19:45.101 --> 19:46.977
-Did you hear that?
-Yes.

19:49.730 --> 19:51.315
We'd broken up a while ago,

19:51.399 --> 19:53.484
but I couldn't find
the right time to tell you.

19:54.568 --> 19:55.569
I see.

19:57.029 --> 19:59.865
The thing is, last time,

20:00.366 --> 20:03.744
I told your boyfriend where to find you.

20:05.830 --> 20:06.956
I messed up, didn't I?

20:07.581 --> 20:09.375
You didn't because you didn't know.

20:09.959 --> 20:11.502
Ignore his calls from now on.

20:11.836 --> 20:13.045
It was a nasty breakup.

20:14.088 --> 20:15.089
Okay.

20:15.172 --> 20:16.298
[phone vibrating]

20:18.050 --> 20:19.218
TEAM LEADER KIM WOOJU

20:22.763 --> 20:23.764
Hello?

20:32.398 --> 20:33.399
[car honks]

20:35.609 --> 20:37.069
Ms. Yoo.

20:47.580 --> 20:48.873
[Kim Wooju chuckles softly]

20:48.956 --> 20:51.292
We'll set off now.

20:51.375 --> 20:52.376
[engine starts]

20:52.460 --> 20:53.961
[♪ gripping, whimsical music playing]

20:57.006 --> 20:58.257
[Meri] Did you get a new car?

20:58.340 --> 20:59.467
[chuckles softly]

20:59.550 --> 21:02.386
I bought it a while ago,
and they just sent it over.

21:03.471 --> 21:04.472
So...

21:05.431 --> 21:07.016
You're my first ever passenger.

21:07.767 --> 21:08.809
[chuckles softly]

21:09.769 --> 21:11.937
It's a lovely car. Quite comfortable, too.

21:12.021 --> 21:13.189
Isn't it?

21:14.231 --> 21:16.025
So, from now on,

21:16.942 --> 21:18.778
I'll pick you up every now and then.

21:19.987 --> 21:20.988
What for?

21:21.071 --> 21:23.908
I just want to treat you better.

21:25.785 --> 21:26.994
[chuckles softly]

21:28.746 --> 21:32.082
I won't fall for sweet-talk like that.

21:32.208 --> 21:34.293
[chuckles softly] I thought so.

21:38.339 --> 21:39.548
[grunts]

21:41.008 --> 21:42.009
What's this?

21:42.718 --> 21:44.261
I picked it up on the way.

21:45.304 --> 21:46.555
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

21:49.850 --> 21:51.352
It's not even my birthday,

21:52.102 --> 21:53.854
-and you got me flowers?
-Yes.

21:57.942 --> 21:59.360
What are these called?

21:59.443 --> 22:01.195
They're white and so round.

22:01.278 --> 22:03.322
They look like cotton balls.

22:03.405 --> 22:06.575
They're called pompons or something.

22:06.659 --> 22:07.785
Pompons?

22:07.868 --> 22:10.246
They have a special meaning
which I don't remember.

22:10.329 --> 22:11.997
You can look it up.

22:13.874 --> 22:15.501
[♪ enchanting orchestral music playing]

22:21.549 --> 22:23.676
POMPON FLOWER SYMBOLISM

22:23.759 --> 22:26.136
[Kim Wooju] My heart is sincere.

22:30.724 --> 22:31.767
[clears throat]

22:38.858 --> 22:39.859
[phone vibrates]

22:40.317 --> 22:42.152
Yes, hello. Where are you?

22:42.236 --> 22:44.530
[♪ soft orchestral music
playing in background]

22:44.613 --> 22:49.660
Oh, you should've said so, then.
We could've rescheduled.

22:52.079 --> 22:53.664
Well...

22:55.416 --> 22:56.584
Okay, I understand.

22:57.209 --> 22:58.210
Bye.

22:59.420 --> 23:00.629
I'm sorry about that.

23:01.672 --> 23:03.340
She can't make it.

23:04.300 --> 23:05.551
Something urgent came up.

23:06.343 --> 23:08.721
I guess she didn't know I'd joined you.

23:09.346 --> 23:10.556
I'll leave, then.

23:10.639 --> 23:12.892
No, don't leave.

23:13.475 --> 23:16.937
She wanted to treat us to say thank you.

23:17.021 --> 23:18.022
You should stay.

23:19.607 --> 23:20.608
Sit back down.

23:20.691 --> 23:21.901
[exclaims]

23:22.610 --> 23:24.695
I can't eat all this on my own.

23:24.778 --> 23:25.779
Sit down.

23:27.072 --> 23:28.365
Come on, take your seat.

23:34.455 --> 23:36.790
You should have a drink with me.

23:46.717 --> 23:47.927
One for you.

23:49.762 --> 23:51.013
One for me.

23:51.096 --> 23:52.306
Cheers.

23:53.807 --> 23:55.392
Come on. Cheers.

24:05.986 --> 24:07.071
[exhales deeply]

24:07.154 --> 24:10.199
It's worth the price. It smells lovely.

24:13.577 --> 24:14.620
[gasps]

24:14.870 --> 24:17.998
Wow, you need to try this, Director.

24:18.082 --> 24:19.208
It's delicious.

24:21.377 --> 24:22.628
Have a taste.

24:32.596 --> 24:35.724
I looked up your interview
to get to know you better.

24:36.350 --> 24:39.687
Oh, you're a pretty competent guy.

24:39.770 --> 24:42.523
You were behind Beauté Department Store's
legendary sales figures,

24:42.606 --> 24:44.441
and became the youngest ever
managing director.

24:44.525 --> 24:45.526
[exclaims in awe]

24:45.609 --> 24:46.610
[inhales deeply]

24:46.694 --> 24:48.404
You have a great character as well.

24:49.738 --> 24:51.365
-Is that praise?
-No.

24:51.448 --> 24:52.658
You're pretty sharp.

24:55.995 --> 24:59.248
I wanted to ask a question,
not praise you.

25:00.499 --> 25:03.669
You chased down and scolded the kids
who were filming in secret,

25:04.712 --> 25:07.006
so you have a sense of justice,

25:07.089 --> 25:09.466
and you seem to be able
to tell right from wrong.

25:10.926 --> 25:13.804
Why are you so intimidated by your boss?

25:18.934 --> 25:20.310
I did some digging.

25:20.394 --> 25:24.606
Whenever your boss needed a doctor's note
to avoid appearing in court,

25:25.149 --> 25:27.026
you got them issued.

25:27.693 --> 25:30.154
That's really unfair of him.

25:34.575 --> 25:35.868
Director.

25:37.077 --> 25:39.246
For a man so competent and just,

25:39.788 --> 25:41.790
doesn't it hurt your pride?

25:42.249 --> 25:43.876
[♪ tense, whimsical music playing]

25:49.548 --> 25:50.841
[chuckles softly]

25:50.924 --> 25:52.843
Did I hit a sore spot?

25:53.427 --> 25:55.512
I'm sorry if I offended you.

25:55.596 --> 25:56.597
There are people

25:56.930 --> 26:01.310
who were born on third base
and think they scored a three-base hit.

26:02.186 --> 26:05.606
They think they got there themselves
and criticize others without thinking.

26:05.689 --> 26:07.024
[♪ gripping, whimsical music playing]

26:07.107 --> 26:10.235
"How incompetent must you be
to struggle at first base?"

26:11.361 --> 26:13.864
The pride and convictions
people like you have...

26:16.116 --> 26:18.118
are the first thing people like me

26:18.911 --> 26:21.330
who struggle to be at first base
must give up.

26:21.914 --> 26:23.123
[♪ whimsical sting]

26:52.361 --> 26:54.113
Oh, right. [clears throat]

26:54.196 --> 26:56.240
I have something for you, too.

26:57.157 --> 27:01.286
You looked after Wooju when I couldn't.

27:01.370 --> 27:04.790
I got this
because I felt sorry and grateful.

27:05.958 --> 27:07.084
Goodness.

27:08.877 --> 27:09.878
Drive safely.

27:10.504 --> 27:11.797
Thanks so much for the flowers.

27:12.464 --> 27:14.550
Wait, this isn't how it goes.

27:15.134 --> 27:18.303
If you're grateful,
you should offer me ramyeon

27:18.387 --> 27:19.555
or at least some water.

27:21.265 --> 27:23.016
I have something to show you, too.

27:23.100 --> 27:24.309
What's that?

27:24.393 --> 27:25.519
DIARY

27:27.396 --> 27:28.438
What's all this?

27:28.522 --> 27:31.733
They say, "Look into their past
if you want to see someone's future."

27:31.817 --> 27:34.444
As you can see, ever since I was seven,

27:34.528 --> 27:37.239
I wrote down how much I spent and whatnot.

27:38.031 --> 27:40.784
I put 1,000 won a day
into a special account,

27:40.868 --> 27:43.453
and I have
countless installment savings accounts.

27:43.537 --> 27:45.706
They say old habits die hard.

27:45.789 --> 27:47.624
People who are used to saving up--

27:47.708 --> 27:52.588
"Today at taekwondo, I did a back kick
and gave my big brother a nosebleed."

27:52.671 --> 27:53.755
[♪ whimsical music playing]

27:53.839 --> 27:56.884
You were always good
at giving people nosebleeds.

27:57.676 --> 27:58.802
You have an older brother?

27:58.886 --> 27:59.887
No, he's my cousin.

27:59.970 --> 28:02.306
Don't read those parts,
and look down here.

28:02.389 --> 28:03.974
"Today's income, today's expense,

28:04.057 --> 28:05.225
-amount saved."
-Okay.

28:05.934 --> 28:07.561
-[clears throat]
-[♪ ethereal sparkle]

28:07.644 --> 28:10.314
I did spend everything I'd saved up
to study abroad,

28:10.397 --> 28:13.066
but anyone who's this diligent
about saving up

28:13.150 --> 28:15.402
will have some basic economic concepts.

28:15.903 --> 28:19.489
I also have an inheritance
my parents left me when they died.

28:19.573 --> 28:21.199
Who is Miso?

28:21.867 --> 28:24.202
"I wonder if she is doing okay.

28:24.286 --> 28:27.581
When I go back to Korea,
I want to thank Miso..."

28:27.664 --> 28:30.375
Why do you keep reading other stuff
instead of what I want you to see?

28:30.459 --> 28:32.336
I can't help it. It's right there.

28:34.296 --> 28:35.547
Who is Miso?

28:36.048 --> 28:37.591
Her name keeps popping up.

28:37.674 --> 28:38.967
She's someone you liked, right?

28:39.051 --> 28:40.135
No.

28:40.218 --> 28:41.637
She is.

28:42.554 --> 28:44.348
Her name might come up again.

28:44.431 --> 28:45.807
Give me that back.

28:46.224 --> 28:47.392
Let me read on.

28:47.476 --> 28:49.811
You shouldn't read someone else's diary--

28:53.732 --> 28:55.651
[slow, rhythmic heartbeats]

28:58.695 --> 29:00.322
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

29:21.885 --> 29:22.970
[stomach rumbles]

29:23.053 --> 29:24.262
[♪ record scratches, music halts]

29:24.346 --> 29:25.389
[stomach rumbling]

29:28.558 --> 29:30.143
I didn't eat dinner yet.

29:31.895 --> 29:33.355
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

29:38.986 --> 29:40.570
[beeps]

29:42.197 --> 29:44.074
[♪ upbeat pop music continues]

29:48.036 --> 29:49.162
[exclaims contentedly]

29:50.414 --> 29:51.748
[both chuckle]

29:52.374 --> 29:54.251
-It's cheese-flavored.
-[acknowledges]

29:55.919 --> 29:56.962
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

29:57.045 --> 29:58.046
Bon appétit.

30:01.466 --> 30:02.467
[hums in satisfaction]

30:03.051 --> 30:04.344
-Is it good?
-It's actual rice cake.

30:04.428 --> 30:06.346
I love rice cakes. It's good.

30:06.430 --> 30:07.973
-I want to try yours.
-Okay.

30:11.685 --> 30:12.811
[Meri] This one's good, too.

30:14.396 --> 30:15.564
[hums in satisfaction]

30:15.647 --> 30:16.940
This would be perfect

30:17.357 --> 30:18.567
-with beer.
-With beer.

30:20.318 --> 30:21.319
Shall we?

30:30.328 --> 30:32.039
I WATCHED A GO MATCH...

30:32.873 --> 30:36.001
I bet you were adorable as a kid.

30:36.084 --> 30:37.335
Was I?

30:38.045 --> 30:40.756
Maybe I was as a kid.

30:41.757 --> 30:42.924
I had to grow up pretty quickly.

30:43.008 --> 30:45.093
What did you want to become?

30:45.177 --> 30:47.304
You mentioned Go in your diary.

30:47.387 --> 30:48.513
[inhales deeply]

30:48.597 --> 30:50.724
That's what I wanted to do
when I was nine.

30:51.391 --> 30:53.185
But after that, [clears throat]

30:53.268 --> 30:56.396
I wanted to be a pilot,
a policeman, a Go player...

30:56.480 --> 30:58.440
I guess I wanted to do
anything that looked cool.

30:59.066 --> 31:01.151
[chuckles] You were greedy.

31:05.739 --> 31:08.867
[clears throat] So, is Miso
the girl you had a crush on?

31:09.785 --> 31:12.412
-Why? Are you bothered?
-No.

31:13.497 --> 31:17.334
You said you didn't have a first love,
but her name cropped up everywhere.

31:17.793 --> 31:19.002
Was it a romance of the century?

31:19.544 --> 31:20.879
Miso isn't her real name.

31:22.756 --> 31:26.259
[sighs]
This is way too embarrassing to explain.

31:26.343 --> 31:27.469
Don't laugh at me.

31:29.137 --> 31:30.138
"Mystery Girl."

31:30.597 --> 31:31.848
Miso's my code for that.

31:31.932 --> 31:33.058
[both chuckle]

31:33.141 --> 31:34.392
[♪ feel-good music playing]

31:34.476 --> 31:36.520
-[coughs]
-You're laughing a bit too hard.

31:36.603 --> 31:37.604
Sorry.

31:39.481 --> 31:40.607
By the way,

31:41.650 --> 31:44.986
why were you so grateful to a girl
you didn't even know?

31:50.283 --> 31:51.535
What is it?

31:51.618 --> 31:52.953
-Tell me.
-[exclaims]

31:53.453 --> 31:54.454
What was that for?

31:54.538 --> 31:56.665
What? I shook really gently.

31:56.748 --> 31:58.333
-[exclaims]
-[chuckles, gasps]

31:58.416 --> 31:59.584
I might end up flying off.

31:59.668 --> 32:01.962
Don't say that.
I shook the chair so gently.

32:02.045 --> 32:04.005
[both laughing]

32:14.266 --> 32:15.725
[gasps, exclaims]

32:25.443 --> 32:26.611
[both exclaim]

32:27.779 --> 32:28.780
I'm okay.

32:29.406 --> 32:30.574
-Okay.
-I'm okay.

32:35.120 --> 32:36.246
I called for a driver.

32:36.872 --> 32:38.915
-Is your car parked over there?
-Yes.

32:41.668 --> 32:42.919
[sighs in exasperation]

32:45.839 --> 32:46.840
[chuckles softly]

32:48.717 --> 32:50.552
Can I ask you something?

32:51.928 --> 32:57.350
But you have to answer super objectively.

32:58.101 --> 33:03.607
Because the people around me
aren't objective.

33:05.275 --> 33:06.276
Do I have

33:07.903 --> 33:10.488
no charm at all as a woman?

33:11.781 --> 33:12.824
[♪ whimsical music playing]

33:12.908 --> 33:13.909
[chuckles nervously]

33:13.992 --> 33:15.952
Tell the honest truth.

33:16.036 --> 33:17.996
Really objectively.

33:20.749 --> 33:22.083
Well, you're not that bad.

33:22.167 --> 33:23.168
[chuckles] Right?

33:23.668 --> 33:25.503
I'm not that bad, am I?

33:26.254 --> 33:27.756
[giggles drunkenly]

33:33.845 --> 33:34.846
[whimpers]

33:36.389 --> 33:37.390
But...

33:38.892 --> 33:41.478
Why doesn't the guy I like

33:42.437 --> 33:44.522
see me as a woman?

33:47.859 --> 33:51.613
Is it because he's known me for too long?

33:52.113 --> 33:53.823
It's not because he's known you for long.

33:54.157 --> 33:57.035
It's because he initially didn't see you
as dating material.

33:57.869 --> 33:58.870
"Initially?"

34:00.163 --> 34:01.289
[giggles]

34:01.623 --> 34:04.459
We met when we were kids.

34:05.794 --> 34:09.089
What would a kid know about dating?

34:09.172 --> 34:11.007
Everyone's a brother or sister

34:11.466 --> 34:13.468
or a friend that's like family.

34:14.094 --> 34:15.720
They might be kids, but they still know.

34:16.221 --> 34:17.514
Especially boys.

34:17.597 --> 34:21.476
They decide right away if someone's
a potential girlfriend or just a sister.

34:22.560 --> 34:23.561
I see.

34:26.731 --> 34:27.732
Then...

34:29.567 --> 34:32.696
he never considered me
a potential date since he was a kid?

34:34.197 --> 34:35.740
Because I had zero charm?

34:35.824 --> 34:37.575
-No, it's--
-Is that it?

34:37.659 --> 34:39.953
No, or maybe yes. That was it.

34:40.412 --> 34:41.413
I see.

34:41.496 --> 34:42.956
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

34:44.666 --> 34:45.917
[crying]

34:51.756 --> 34:55.093
Kim Wooju, you son of a b****!

34:58.430 --> 35:00.432
You told me to be objectively honest.

35:00.515 --> 35:01.766
[wailing]

35:03.184 --> 35:04.185
[sighs]

35:10.358 --> 35:11.359
[gasps]

35:12.902 --> 35:14.154
My car's here.

35:14.237 --> 35:15.322
That is my car.

35:15.989 --> 35:17.198
[Jingyeong] It's my car.

35:17.282 --> 35:18.450
-It's mine.
-I should

35:19.159 --> 35:20.535
get back home now.

35:20.619 --> 35:21.911
[♪ gripping, comical music playing]

35:21.995 --> 35:23.330
Get back safely.

35:23.413 --> 35:26.249
No, but that's my car. Hello?

35:26.333 --> 35:28.001
-Jingyeong's car.
-Just a moment.

35:28.084 --> 35:29.127
[phone vibrating]

35:29.669 --> 35:31.755
Hello? Is this the driver for hire?

35:33.548 --> 35:35.717
You can't call me now
to say you can't come.

35:37.636 --> 35:38.637
[scoffs]

35:40.096 --> 35:41.097
Okay, fine.

35:42.599 --> 35:44.726
-Jingyeong's car.
-Hey, wait.

35:50.815 --> 35:51.816
[Jingyeong grunts]

35:53.318 --> 35:54.903
[♪ dramatic sting]

35:56.404 --> 35:57.405
Hello?

36:00.033 --> 36:01.034
This is my car, Doctor.

36:04.079 --> 36:05.330
Doctor.

36:05.789 --> 36:06.790
Hey.

36:07.374 --> 36:10.085
Call if there's an emergency case.

36:10.710 --> 36:11.711
Ms. Yoon.

36:12.879 --> 36:13.922
Ms. Yoon.

36:14.714 --> 36:16.257
Ms. Yoon, you...

36:19.344 --> 36:20.637
[Jingyeong slurring]

36:22.847 --> 36:25.016
I'm sorry, sir.
I thought she was with you.

36:27.811 --> 36:28.853
[sighs in exasperation]

36:30.105 --> 36:31.481
It's so hot.

36:33.024 --> 36:34.109
[groans softly]

36:36.653 --> 36:37.696
[sighs]

36:42.242 --> 36:43.243
[gasps]

36:43.660 --> 36:45.537
It doesn't look good.
It's raining even harder.

36:47.497 --> 36:48.498
CANCEL REQUEST

36:49.207 --> 36:50.333
Did you find a driver?

36:50.417 --> 36:52.043
No, not yet.

36:52.127 --> 36:55.380
Why is it so hard to find someone?
Is it because it's raining so hard?

36:55.463 --> 36:56.756
THE REQUEST WAS CANCELED

37:01.428 --> 37:05.598
Why is it so hard to match with a driver
when it's not even rush hour?

37:06.516 --> 37:08.560
It might be harder
because we're on the outskirts.

37:08.643 --> 37:10.478
Yes, I guess.

37:10.562 --> 37:11.604
[inhales deeply]

37:11.688 --> 37:13.898
What should I do now?

37:13.982 --> 37:15.316
I can't stay the night.

37:16.192 --> 37:17.736
You can stay the night.

37:17.819 --> 37:19.112
There are plenty of bedrooms.

37:19.195 --> 37:21.656
And it's your house, too.

37:22.365 --> 37:23.366
-What?
-What?

37:23.658 --> 37:24.826
[♪ whimsical music playing]

37:24.909 --> 37:27.912
I mean, that's what we told
the department store,

37:27.996 --> 37:31.374
and you helped me out,
so you have a big share in the house.

37:31.458 --> 37:33.793
Oh, yes. That's true.
Then I'll stay the night.

37:33.877 --> 37:35.003
-You can.
-Okay.

37:36.004 --> 37:37.881
How will you get to work tomorrow?

37:38.506 --> 37:39.924
I can leave really early.

37:40.008 --> 37:41.092
Yes, right.

37:41.176 --> 37:43.011
The rain will have stopped by then.

37:43.094 --> 37:45.388
-And I'll be sober by then.
-Yes.

37:47.682 --> 37:48.767
[Meri hums thoughtfully]

37:49.350 --> 37:50.935
Where will you sleep, then?

37:56.733 --> 37:57.776
[hums thoughtfully]

37:59.986 --> 38:01.529
That room...

38:01.613 --> 38:03.656
-I'll sleep here.
-What?

38:04.157 --> 38:05.450
Why here? There are bedrooms.

38:05.533 --> 38:06.576
I prefer the couch.

38:06.659 --> 38:07.994
Excuse me.

38:08.077 --> 38:09.537
[chuckles] You can't sleep out here.

38:10.121 --> 38:11.456
-I can.
-It's too uncomfortable.

38:11.539 --> 38:12.540
-Let me--
-It's fine.

38:12.624 --> 38:14.334
Let me find you something comfy
to change into.

38:14.417 --> 38:15.460
Oh, okay.

38:15.543 --> 38:17.128
[inhales deeply, clears throat]

38:18.546 --> 38:19.589
[clears throat]

38:20.298 --> 38:21.549
[sighing contentedly]

38:24.928 --> 38:27.305
Something comfy he can wear...

38:30.850 --> 38:31.976
Oh, yes.

38:37.899 --> 38:38.900
[inhales deeply]

38:41.778 --> 38:42.904
[rain pattering]

38:46.699 --> 38:48.451
Mr. Kim. I found you a...

38:51.037 --> 38:52.622
[♪ gentle pop music playing]

39:41.629 --> 39:42.672
[chuckles softly]

39:43.548 --> 39:45.300
He looks precious when he's asleep.

40:24.547 --> 40:27.300
It feels like a couple sleeping apart
after an argument.

40:31.512 --> 40:32.555
[chuckles softly]

40:42.023 --> 40:43.107
[thunderclap]

40:43.191 --> 40:44.609
My goodness.

40:47.195 --> 40:48.279
That really got me.

40:50.740 --> 40:53.076
-[thunder rumbling]
-[rain pattering]

41:08.466 --> 41:09.509
[grunts softly]

41:13.179 --> 41:14.222
[tapping]

41:14.847 --> 41:15.932
[vibrates]

41:21.646 --> 41:22.647
[Kim Wooju] Are you asleep?

41:23.022 --> 41:24.148
[Meri] No, not yet.

41:24.232 --> 41:26.025
[thunder rumbling]

41:26.109 --> 41:27.777
The thunder and lightning
are really scary.

41:27.860 --> 41:28.861
[chuckles softly]

41:28.945 --> 41:30.154
[♪ heartfelt piano music playing]

41:30.238 --> 41:31.906
[Kim Wooju] Yes.

41:31.990 --> 41:33.199
It startled you, didn't it?

41:34.701 --> 41:35.702
[Meri] A little.

41:39.831 --> 41:40.873
[phone chimes]

41:42.083 --> 41:43.418
TEAM LEADER KIM WOOJU

41:43.501 --> 41:44.711
UNDER THE LONELY SKY, English Ver

41:47.505 --> 41:48.673
[♪ song plays]

42:45.313 --> 42:46.939
[♪ song fades]

42:47.023 --> 42:48.399
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

42:48.483 --> 42:50.526
[♪ gentle piano music
playing in background]

42:52.445 --> 42:54.781
You said Mr. Baek invited us
to breakfast once.

42:54.864 --> 42:56.365
Let him see us while I'm here.

42:56.449 --> 42:59.660
Is that why you wanted us
to wear the same shirts?

43:00.161 --> 43:01.829
You said we had to play the part.

43:03.831 --> 43:05.792
When does he come here to eat anyway?

43:06.417 --> 43:08.086
I don't know.

43:08.753 --> 43:10.129
Hey, over there.

43:12.715 --> 43:13.925
-Look.
-Let's move.

43:16.427 --> 43:17.428
[chuckles softly]

43:22.141 --> 43:23.267
Yes.

43:23.351 --> 43:25.478
The women's wear samples we got last week.

43:26.437 --> 43:28.189
Can you bring me a few items?

43:29.440 --> 43:30.942
Average height, slim build.

43:31.943 --> 43:32.944
Yes, right away.

43:34.695 --> 43:36.489
-[line disconnects]
-[Meri] Mr. Baek.

43:36.572 --> 43:38.157
Good morning.

43:38.241 --> 43:40.618
Oh, hi. Are you here for breakfast?

43:40.701 --> 43:44.747
My wife insisted we check out the place,
so here we are.

43:44.831 --> 43:47.333
I see. You can take this table. I'm done.

43:48.292 --> 43:49.710
You're done already?

43:49.794 --> 43:52.046
We were hoping to eat with you.

43:52.839 --> 43:54.632
Some other time, maybe.

43:55.842 --> 43:58.094
I'll see you around, then.

43:58.177 --> 43:59.637
[Meri] It's a bummer.

44:04.725 --> 44:06.102
-[cutlery clatters]
-[giggles]

44:07.937 --> 44:08.938
Let's eat.

44:09.647 --> 44:10.648
[snoring]

44:10.731 --> 44:12.275
[♪ gripping, comical music playing]

44:16.904 --> 44:17.905
[grunts softly]

44:21.367 --> 44:22.493
[exclaims, grunts]

44:23.911 --> 44:24.912
[groans]

44:26.455 --> 44:28.541
[exclaiming in pain] Jeez.

44:39.427 --> 44:40.469
[grunts softly]

44:41.804 --> 44:44.015
Yoon Jingyeong, family medicine.

44:44.557 --> 44:45.725
Is it an emergency?

44:51.105 --> 44:52.148
Darn it.

45:00.573 --> 45:01.574
What's this?

45:02.491 --> 45:03.701
Where am I?

45:14.545 --> 45:15.588
[gasps]

45:15.671 --> 45:17.173
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

45:17.256 --> 45:18.549
I look horrible.

45:20.843 --> 45:21.844
[gasps]

45:23.512 --> 45:24.805
What am I wearing?

45:25.056 --> 45:27.058
-[exclaiming excitedly]
-[Sanghyeon exclaiming in pain]

45:29.852 --> 45:32.605
This is so high! I'm high up!

45:32.688 --> 45:33.940
-[grunts]
-[panting]

45:34.023 --> 45:35.942
I was having fun.

45:37.735 --> 45:39.654
A round ball.

45:39.946 --> 45:41.155
[bellowing]

45:42.865 --> 45:43.991
[grunts]

45:44.492 --> 45:45.701
[Jingyeong mumbling]

45:48.371 --> 45:49.372
[Jingyeong exclaims]

45:53.000 --> 45:56.295
-[sighs in exasperation]
-It's so warm in here. I feel so hot.

45:56.629 --> 45:57.964
[exclaiming drunkenly]

45:59.966 --> 46:01.467
What are you doing now?

46:01.550 --> 46:03.594
-I can't see!
-Ms. Yoon!

46:03.678 --> 46:05.429
-Ms. Yoon.
-[screams]

46:05.888 --> 46:07.014
[groaning]

46:08.557 --> 46:09.892
My head hurts.

46:10.935 --> 46:12.520
Am I a blockhead?

46:12.603 --> 46:13.646
Ms. Yoon.

46:13.729 --> 46:15.982
-[exclaiming drunkenly]
-[exclaiming anxiously]

46:17.066 --> 46:18.192
[Jingyeong screams]

46:19.735 --> 46:20.945
[Jingyeong panting]

46:22.780 --> 46:24.448
[breathing heavily]

46:32.790 --> 46:33.833
[gags]

46:33.916 --> 46:35.459
[♪ dramatic guitar music playing]

46:36.711 --> 46:39.046
No, don't! [grunts, exclaims anxiously]

46:39.130 --> 46:40.506
[Jingyeong] The bathroom!

46:40.589 --> 46:41.590
[Sanghyeon] Wait.

46:43.050 --> 46:44.885
-The bathroom!
-The bathroom.

46:44.969 --> 46:46.762
The bathroom's over here!

46:46.846 --> 46:48.764
Now you can puke! [panting]

46:49.724 --> 46:50.808
[gasps in horror]

46:52.560 --> 46:53.936
[whines in embarrassment]

46:58.524 --> 47:00.443
[♪ dramatic sting]

47:02.820 --> 47:04.155
[door keypad beeping]

47:04.613 --> 47:05.698
[door unlocks]

47:05.781 --> 47:07.199
[♪ dramatic music continues]

47:13.789 --> 47:15.124
[♪ dramatic sting]

47:19.170 --> 47:20.171
[gasps]

47:27.845 --> 47:29.472
I sent your clothes to the dry cleaners,

47:29.555 --> 47:31.307
and I can get them back this afternoon.

47:31.807 --> 47:34.393
So, I found you something to change into.

47:34.852 --> 47:36.604
-[Jingyeong] Okay.
-I'm...

47:37.855 --> 47:38.856
leaving for work.

47:39.940 --> 47:41.150
[Jingyeong acknowledges softly]

47:42.651 --> 47:43.986
Here's some hangover soup.

47:48.783 --> 47:49.950
[door opens, lock beeps]

47:51.160 --> 47:53.037
[♪ gripping, whimsical music playing]

47:54.330 --> 47:55.331
[sighs sheepishly]

47:55.414 --> 47:56.874
[whines in embarrassment]

47:58.542 --> 47:59.543
[sighs]

48:00.378 --> 48:01.379
[pants]

48:02.463 --> 48:03.464
[gasps]

48:03.547 --> 48:06.050
Yoon Jingyeong, you lost your mind!

48:06.133 --> 48:07.968
[whines in embarrassment]

48:10.054 --> 48:12.348
-[clears throat]
-Shall we have a coffee?

48:12.431 --> 48:14.100
Yes, sure. Here is...

48:19.980 --> 48:21.023
Hey.

48:25.444 --> 48:26.445
Hey.

48:26.779 --> 48:28.280
[♪ enchanting dreamy music playing]

48:30.282 --> 48:31.367
[exclaims]

48:37.164 --> 48:38.290
[gasps]

48:39.792 --> 48:41.710
Isn't that Oh Sanguk?

48:41.794 --> 48:43.546
[Meri] No way. [gasps]

48:43.629 --> 48:45.756
Where... [sighs]

48:46.715 --> 48:48.008
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

48:49.760 --> 48:50.761
[hesitates]

48:51.262 --> 48:53.681
Hello, are you...

48:53.764 --> 48:56.517
-It's you, right?
-Yes, that's me.

48:56.600 --> 48:57.643
[exclaims excitedly]

48:58.519 --> 48:59.979
I'm a huge fan of yours.

49:00.062 --> 49:01.939
-You were awesome in Paris.
-[Kim Wooju] My goodness.

49:02.022 --> 49:04.442
-Someone's really excited.
-[Meri] You're incredible.

49:05.192 --> 49:06.193
Do you mind

49:06.277 --> 49:08.654
-giving me an autograph?
-That's fine.

49:08.737 --> 49:11.198
-What do we have...
-We don't have a pen.

49:11.824 --> 49:12.825
[Sanguk] I have one.

49:12.908 --> 49:14.827
Then can you sign this for me?

49:14.910 --> 49:16.287
-Your shirt?
-Yes.

49:16.787 --> 49:17.788
No, wait.

49:19.081 --> 49:20.791
-Sign mine instead.
-Okay.

49:20.875 --> 49:22.626
-I'll sign on the back.
-Yes.

49:25.963 --> 49:27.548
You're so good-looking.

49:27.631 --> 49:29.258
Wow, your shoulders are so broad.

49:29.341 --> 49:30.468
[♪ upbeat dreamy music playing]

49:30.551 --> 49:31.594
-Thanks.
-[giggles]

49:31.677 --> 49:32.720
What's your name?

49:32.803 --> 49:33.804
It's Yoo Meri.

49:35.014 --> 49:36.807
[Kim Wooju] She's delighted.

49:42.897 --> 49:43.898
I'm done.

49:44.982 --> 49:46.192
Thank you.

49:46.275 --> 49:47.610
Thank you so much.

49:47.693 --> 49:50.654
If you don't mind,
can I take a photo with you?

49:50.738 --> 49:51.906
Why not?

49:51.989 --> 49:53.991
-[squeals] A photo!
-Why ask for a photo, too?

49:54.074 --> 49:55.159
[exclaims excitedly]

50:00.498 --> 50:01.874
No, not like that.

50:05.336 --> 50:06.629
Are you ready?

50:06.712 --> 50:08.130
One, two, three.

50:08.589 --> 50:09.673
[camera shutter clicks]

50:09.757 --> 50:12.510
Take one more picture. Just one more.

50:16.847 --> 50:18.641
One, two, three.

50:18.724 --> 50:19.725
[camera shutter clicks]

50:23.812 --> 50:25.773
-Thank you.
-Sure.

50:25.856 --> 50:26.857
Bye, then.

50:26.941 --> 50:28.400
-Good luck.
-You too.

50:41.080 --> 50:42.665
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

50:56.303 --> 50:57.304
[sighs softly]

51:00.015 --> 51:01.308
Let's have a look.

51:09.525 --> 51:10.693
What's this?

51:10.776 --> 51:11.777
What's what?

51:12.403 --> 51:14.572
What the heck? What happened?

51:14.655 --> 51:16.282
[♪ whimsical sting]

51:16.365 --> 51:17.825
The backlight's too strong. [chuckles]

51:17.908 --> 51:19.076
Oh, too bad.

51:19.660 --> 51:21.745
[scoffs] Did you do that on purpose?

51:21.829 --> 51:24.415
I did not. What do you take me for?

51:25.040 --> 51:26.250
I'll get a better one next time.

51:26.333 --> 51:27.710
It was on purpose.

51:29.503 --> 51:30.796
Wait for me.

51:32.631 --> 51:34.341
I'll take another one for you next time.

51:34.425 --> 51:36.343
There won't be a next time.

51:36.427 --> 51:38.220
-I'll ask him to--
-[Meri] Forget it.

51:38.304 --> 51:39.346
[Kim Wooju] Come on.

51:39.763 --> 51:41.390
[♪ gripping, dramatic music playing]

51:42.850 --> 51:44.727
-Wooju.
-Jingyeong.

51:56.071 --> 51:57.615
IT WAS A PLEASURE TO MEET YOU, YOO MERI!

51:57.698 --> 51:58.991
OH SANGUK

52:00.034 --> 52:01.452
Have you lost your mind?

52:02.077 --> 52:03.996
What if your grandmother finds out?

52:04.079 --> 52:06.540
I didn't think it would snowball.

52:07.082 --> 52:09.752
But it's true that Ms. Yoo won the raffle.

52:10.210 --> 52:12.046
-Things just got messed up.
-Whatever.

52:12.129 --> 52:13.672
Back out of it right now.

52:14.214 --> 52:15.507
You've gone crazy.

52:15.591 --> 52:17.843
This makes you an accomplice.

52:17.926 --> 52:19.637
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

52:32.483 --> 52:33.609
[line ringing]

52:33.984 --> 52:36.153
Hello, sir, this is Kim Juhee.

52:37.112 --> 52:39.448
I have a question
regarding the consulting firm

52:39.531 --> 52:41.492
we hired to enter the US market.

52:42.159 --> 52:44.995
I found nothing wrong
with the contract I looked over last time.

52:47.206 --> 52:48.290
Let me look into it.

52:48.791 --> 52:49.792
Bye.

52:49.875 --> 52:51.001
CFO
JANG HANGU

52:51.085 --> 52:52.086
[line disconnects]

52:53.754 --> 52:55.881
It looks like Ms. Kim noticed something.

52:55.964 --> 52:57.508
[♪ ominous music playing]

52:59.927 --> 53:01.387
[♪ music crescendos, halts]

53:02.888 --> 53:06.517
I'm waiting for confirmation
on the color of the sheet mask package.

53:06.600 --> 53:08.477
If the client makes any extra requests,

53:08.560 --> 53:10.813
just tell me,
and I'll handle it when I get back.

53:10.896 --> 53:13.899
Shall I say you went home
for your father's death anniversary?

53:13.982 --> 53:15.109
If it might help.

53:15.192 --> 53:16.360
Are you leaving soon?

53:16.443 --> 53:17.569
[inhales deeply]

53:18.821 --> 53:21.240
I still have some time left.

53:21.323 --> 53:22.616
[phone ringing]

53:23.492 --> 53:24.910
INCOMING CALL

53:26.578 --> 53:27.579
Hello?

53:28.706 --> 53:30.499
[♪ soft, somber music playing]

53:32.918 --> 53:35.087
I probably surprised you
by suddenly reaching out.

53:36.797 --> 53:38.090
No, not at all.

53:38.173 --> 53:39.925
I meant to call you, too.

53:41.593 --> 53:44.847
Do you know why I called?

53:44.930 --> 53:47.933
-Yes.
-Then I won't drag this on.

53:48.016 --> 53:50.185
Leave Wooju out of it.

53:51.520 --> 53:54.523
I know... I should.

53:54.606 --> 53:57.109
He can't afford to get involved
with something like that.

53:57.192 --> 54:01.113
People would talk nonstop
if this were to get out.

54:02.614 --> 54:04.158
He has a company to inherit.

54:05.617 --> 54:06.744
A company?

54:06.827 --> 54:08.537
Didn't you know?

54:14.334 --> 54:17.004
He's the grandson of Myungsoondang's CEO.

54:18.130 --> 54:20.549
He'll take over the company later on.

54:20.632 --> 54:22.092
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

54:23.594 --> 54:24.595
I...

54:26.138 --> 54:28.390
I really had no idea.

54:28.932 --> 54:31.143
I shouldn't have involved him
even if I'd known, but...

54:31.226 --> 54:32.895
Oh, dear. I feel so bad.

54:34.313 --> 54:38.317
I was in such a bad situation
that I only thought of myself.

54:40.778 --> 54:42.780
I'll talk to Mr. Kim about it.

54:42.863 --> 54:46.116
Can't you just end it on your end, Meri?

54:47.409 --> 54:50.454
Wooju won't be able to say no to you.

54:50.871 --> 54:52.456
Because he owes you.

54:53.999 --> 54:55.501
He owes me?

54:58.754 --> 54:59.838
[sighs softly]

54:59.922 --> 55:01.340
[♪ ominous sting]

55:05.802 --> 55:07.721
[Jingyeong] Didn't you know

55:07.804 --> 55:10.057
that your father saved Wooju that day?

55:10.140 --> 55:12.559
-I was driving from that direction...
-[young Kim Wooju] Dad!

55:12.643 --> 55:13.727
...when I saw him

55:13.810 --> 55:15.854
-standing on the road looking like that.
-Mom!

55:15.938 --> 55:20.192
-That's when I stepped on the brakes.
-Dad!

55:20.275 --> 55:23.070
[crying] I'm sorry!

55:23.946 --> 55:25.572
That boy was Mr. Kim.

55:25.656 --> 55:27.407
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

55:30.202 --> 55:31.411
He should've said so.

55:32.955 --> 55:35.207
[Jingyeong] That's why he helped you out.

55:36.041 --> 55:37.042
Because he felt bad.

55:37.584 --> 55:39.086
He wanted to pay you back.

55:43.173 --> 55:44.925
Who is Miso?

55:45.551 --> 55:49.805
"If time passes
and I see Miso again one day,

55:50.681 --> 55:53.100
I should tell her I'm sorry."

55:55.477 --> 55:56.728
Now I understand.

56:04.278 --> 56:07.197
[voice over PA system]
The bus to Yeosu will leave shortly.

56:07.281 --> 56:08.991
Please board the bus.

56:16.164 --> 56:18.333
[♪ gentle piano music
playing in background]

56:21.670 --> 56:22.671
Jingyeong.

56:24.214 --> 56:26.049
-Hey, you're here.
-[chuckles softly]

56:26.675 --> 56:28.510
Why did you suddenly want to see me?

56:30.012 --> 56:31.013
Well...

56:35.434 --> 56:37.019
What is it?

56:43.900 --> 56:46.570
Wooju, I messed up.

56:48.155 --> 56:49.156
What?

56:50.032 --> 56:51.366
I told Meri everything.

56:51.992 --> 56:53.327
I told her to stop using you...

56:53.410 --> 56:54.828
[♪ enthralling tense music playing]

56:56.038 --> 56:57.039
[sighs]

56:57.331 --> 56:58.332
Wooju.

57:00.709 --> 57:01.752
[sighs]

57:05.172 --> 57:06.298
[line ringing]

57:20.520 --> 57:22.606
-[line continues ringing]
-[engine starts]

57:23.649 --> 57:24.691
[tires screech]

57:34.451 --> 57:36.787
[Youngsook] Here you go.

57:40.874 --> 57:41.875
[sighs]

57:43.460 --> 57:44.461
[grunts]

57:44.795 --> 57:48.674
Sundol has been stressed out.

57:48.757 --> 57:50.300
He eats so much.

57:50.384 --> 57:52.427
What would he be stressed out about?

57:52.511 --> 57:54.179
Aesun from next door. [chuckles]

57:54.429 --> 57:55.847
Sundol thought she liked him,

57:55.931 --> 57:59.101
and got his hopes up,
but she mated with another dog.

57:59.976 --> 58:02.062
He didn't eat for a few days,

58:02.145 --> 58:04.356
but now he won't stop eating.

58:04.439 --> 58:08.819
Man, he's not cute anymore
because he's gotten so lazy and chubby.

58:08.902 --> 58:10.028
I hate it.

58:10.112 --> 58:12.280
Gosh, the poor thing.

58:12.364 --> 58:13.532
Don't feel bad for him.

58:13.615 --> 58:16.034
He ruined his life
by getting his hopes up.

58:16.118 --> 58:17.327
That's pitiful.

58:17.411 --> 58:18.537
[wet fabric squishes]

58:20.956 --> 58:22.874
-Are you hungry?
-No, I'm fine.

58:25.460 --> 58:26.461
Is something wrong?

58:27.921 --> 58:29.089
Nothing's wrong.

58:31.091 --> 58:33.468
[sighs] I should take Sundol for a walk.

58:39.850 --> 58:40.851
Come along.

58:44.396 --> 58:45.981
That brat.

58:46.064 --> 58:48.150
What's up with her now?

58:52.320 --> 58:53.613
[phone vibrating]

58:53.905 --> 58:55.782
TEAM LEADER KIM WOOJU

58:55.866 --> 58:57.451
[♪ poignant, melancholy music playing]

59:01.246 --> 59:04.708
You know, Sundol.
You need to calm down a bit.

59:05.959 --> 59:08.211
You get carried away too easily.

59:09.838 --> 59:10.839
[sighs]

59:11.882 --> 59:14.968
You can't give your heart that easily.

59:15.427 --> 59:16.887
That's how you get hurt.

59:18.638 --> 59:20.015
[chuckles softly] Hey, boy.

59:20.974 --> 59:23.268
Being cute isn't a free pass.

59:27.731 --> 59:28.940
From now on,

59:29.900 --> 59:31.902
even if someone says they like you,

59:31.985 --> 59:34.571
you need to stay calm, okay?

59:35.155 --> 59:39.534
Life isn't all sunshine
and rainbows, you know.

59:40.368 --> 59:41.828
Do you get that?

59:53.173 --> 59:54.216
[car door closes]

59:57.344 --> 59:59.012
Why didn't you answer your phone?

59:59.721 --> 01:00:00.722
What?

01:00:02.098 --> 01:00:04.726
Oh, I must've left it at home.

01:00:08.605 --> 01:00:09.648
[chuckles softly]

01:00:10.565 --> 01:00:12.067
[♪ dreamy, ambient music playing]

01:00:34.422 --> 01:00:37.259
Why didn't you tell me
you met up with Jingyeong?

01:00:40.053 --> 01:00:41.888
I was going to tell you.

01:00:42.430 --> 01:00:44.182
When? Next year?

01:00:49.271 --> 01:00:52.107
Don't you want to ask me anything?

01:00:53.316 --> 01:00:54.359
[hesitates]

01:00:56.987 --> 01:00:58.113
[inhales deeply]

01:00:59.489 --> 01:01:01.783
Do you still have the stuffed toy
I gave you?

01:01:02.534 --> 01:01:04.452
Yes, I've been keeping it safe.

01:01:06.454 --> 01:01:07.539
[exclaims]

01:01:08.999 --> 01:01:10.000
What else?

01:01:12.294 --> 01:01:14.421
[clears throat] In your old diary,

01:01:15.505 --> 01:01:16.965
am I the Mystery Girl?

01:01:18.133 --> 01:01:19.217
Yes.

01:01:27.017 --> 01:01:29.436
There's something else you want to ask.

01:01:39.738 --> 01:01:40.739
I'm fine.

01:01:42.824 --> 01:01:43.825
With what?

01:01:44.326 --> 01:01:46.077
My dad's death.

01:01:47.120 --> 01:01:49.205
I don't blame your family for it.

01:01:51.291 --> 01:01:53.084
While my dad was alive,

01:01:54.961 --> 01:01:57.172
he loved me very much.

01:01:59.090 --> 01:02:00.091
So...

01:02:06.681 --> 01:02:08.892
So you don't have to feel bad.

01:02:15.649 --> 01:02:16.650
Also,

01:02:17.359 --> 01:02:19.194
you can stop helping me.

01:02:19.277 --> 01:02:21.863
It's not just about what Jingyeong said.

01:02:23.907 --> 01:02:27.369
Honestly, I've been
feeling uneasy about it too.

01:02:30.789 --> 01:02:32.248
It's not because I'm sorry.

01:02:34.334 --> 01:02:35.585
It's because I like you.

01:02:39.297 --> 01:02:41.007
I'm doing this because I like you.

01:02:42.550 --> 01:02:44.469
Whatever it is that you do,

01:02:45.428 --> 01:02:47.222
I'll stay right next to you.

01:02:48.348 --> 01:02:49.599
[♪ gentle, dreamy music playing]

01:02:57.649 --> 01:02:58.858
So...

01:03:37.313 --> 01:03:38.648
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

01:04:04.924 --> 01:04:07.594
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:04:07.677 --> 01:04:09.721
[Meri] You never came back
to Korea all that time?

01:04:09.804 --> 01:04:12.348
[Kim Wooju] I did. I came to see you.

01:04:12.432 --> 01:04:14.851
[Youngsook] If your family
mistreats my Meri,

01:04:14.934 --> 01:04:16.269
I won't let her marry you.

01:04:16.352 --> 01:04:19.272
Even if it's just for a day,
she should live feeling loved.

01:04:19.355 --> 01:04:21.816
[Meri] I'm going to tell
Mr. Baek everything.

01:04:21.900 --> 01:04:24.152
[Sanghyeon] Don't blame yourself.
All people are selfish.

01:04:24.235 --> 01:04:26.112
[Wooju] He's the grandson
of Myungsoondang's CEO.

01:04:26.196 --> 01:04:28.156
End it unless you want to see him go down!

01:04:29.407 --> 01:04:31.076
[Philnyun] Are things going well
with Wooju?

01:04:31.659 --> 01:04:34.370
[Meri] Will coming clean
improve my chances with you?

01:04:34.454 --> 01:04:35.789
[Kim Wooju] What are you saying?

01:04:35.872 --> 01:04:36.956
Do you want us to break up?

01:04:40.835 --> 01:04:42.837
Translated by Jennifer Jean Lim
